  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run `vite build` or render a frame, so I haven't seen the scene. The ring orientation, lighting levels and framing are untested.\n\n- **Star and bloom:** a 2.4-unit glowing star sits at the centre with a point light inside it. Bloom is applied to the whole frame. The background is near-black (`#02030a`) with 220 small seeded stars.\n- **Planets:** five planets of different sizes and colours orbit on radii 3.4, 5.2, 7.2, 9.2 and 11. Each has its own angular speed. Faint orbit lines are drawn on the ground plane.\n- **Ring:** the fourth planet (`saturn`) has a tilted, double-sided ring that moves with it.\n- **Animation and camera:** planet positions are updated every frame in `app.onFrame` from accumulated `dt`. The camera is at `[0, 17, 18]` looking at the origin with a 45° field of view, chosen so the outermost orbit should fit in the 640x360 canvas.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nI didn't call `requestAnimationFrame` for the render loop myself. `createAuraApp` runs that loop.\n\n",
